    "subject_name": "Mathematics",
    "chapter_id": "616025301bea759b280026c5",
    "chapter_name": "Binomial Theorem",
    "year": "2023",
    "shift": "shift_1"
  },
  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, be the smallest number such that the expansion of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mn>30</mn></msup></math> has a term <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#946;</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>N</mi></math>. Then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> is equal to _____ ."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>General term of the binomial expansion of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mn>30</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mi>r</mi><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>30</mn></mmultiscripts><msup><mfenced><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mfenced><mrow><mn>30</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac></mfenced><mi>r</mi></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mi>r</mi><none/><mprescripts/><none/><mn>30</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi></msup><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>60</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>11</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msup></math></p><p>So, for term of the form&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#946;</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></msup></math>, we have</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>60</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>11</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>11</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>60</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mfrac><mn>60</mn><mn>11</mn></mfrac><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p><p>So,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>6</mn><none/><mprescripts/><none/><mn>30</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>6</mn></msup><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>We have also observed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>=</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>6</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>30</mn></mmultiscripts><msup><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mn>6</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;is a natural number.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p>"
  }
}